From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pmaports <pmaports@localhost>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 08:54:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] ASoC: cs35l41: don't fail power-up when PUP/PDN status
 never comes

Both amps on the Xiaomi Mi 10 never set the PUP/PDN done bits but power up and play. Warn and carry on instead of failing the DAPM event with -ETIMEDOUT. Same idea as the bring-up's cs35l41-ignore-pup-poll.
---
 sound/soc/codecs/cs35l41-lib.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l41-lib.c b/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l41-lib.c
index 1702f2604..719e40117 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l41-lib.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l41-lib.c
@@ -1269,8 +1269,16 @@ int cs35l41_global_enable(struct device *dev, struct regmap *regmap, enum cs35l4
 		ret = regmap_read_poll_timeout(regmap, CS35L41_IRQ1_STATUS1,
 					int_status, int_status & pup_pdn_mask,
 					1000, 100000);
-		if (ret)
-			dev_err(dev, "Enable(%d) failed: %d\n", enable, ret);
+		if (ret) {
+			/*
+			 * The two amps on the Xiaomi Mi 10 never raise the
+			 * PUP/PDN done bits, yet power up and play fine.
+			 * Don't fail the DAPM event over it.
+			 */
+			dev_warn(dev, "Enable(%d): no PUP/PDN status (%d), continuing\n",
+				 enable, ret);
+			ret = 0;
+		}
 
 		/* Clear PUP/PDN status */
 		regmap_write(regmap, CS35L41_IRQ1_STATUS1, pup_pdn_mask);
@@ -1286,8 +1294,16 @@ int cs35l41_global_enable(struct device *dev, struct regmap *regmap, enum cs35l4
 		ret = regmap_read_poll_timeout(regmap, CS35L41_IRQ1_STATUS1,
 					int_status, int_status & pup_pdn_mask,
 					1000, 100000);
-		if (ret)
-			dev_err(dev, "Enable(%d) failed: %d\n", enable, ret);
+		if (ret) {
+			/*
+			 * The two amps on the Xiaomi Mi 10 never raise the
+			 * PUP/PDN done bits, yet power up and play fine.
+			 * Don't fail the DAPM event over it.
+			 */
+			dev_warn(dev, "Enable(%d): no PUP/PDN status (%d), continuing\n",
+				 enable, ret);
+			ret = 0;
+		}
 
 		/* Clear PUP/PDN status */
 		regmap_write(regmap, CS35L41_IRQ1_STATUS1, pup_pdn_mask);
